a great-grandmother's family is suing  Alaska Airlines after she tumbled down  an escalator in the Portland Oregon  Airport the troubling incident was  caught on video the 75 year old woman in  a wheelchair died three months after the  fall that left her badly injured Adriana  Diaz is here with the allegations and  the airlines response  Adriana good morning good morning the  family of Bernice Kerr Kona hired help  to make sure she arrived safely to her  connecting flight but now they're suing  arguing that the airline and its  contractor did not provide the service  as promised  Bernice Kona was coming home from a  family vacation in Maui she landed in  Portland and the family's attorney says  they requested a wheelchair assistance  service to escort her to a connecting  flight but surveillance video shows her  wandering the terminal alone attorney  Brooke Cunningham she was provided  assistance off the airplane and into her  wheelchair by Alaska's company that they  contract with Huntley and then she was  left there and she became confused and  that led to the fall Gakona appeared to  confuse the escalator for an elevator  she fell down headfirst while others  tried to help her the attorney took  video statements from family members  Kona suffered multiple injuries she was  in constant pain  a wound on her right foot became  infected leading to amputation below the  knee a day after that surgery Kaukauna  died all they needed was somebody to use  the escort service that they're required  by law to provide she would have been  perfectly fine Alaska Airlines said in a  statement it appears that Miska Kona  declined ongoing assistance in the  terminal and decided to proceed on her  own to her connecting flight the airline  also noted her reservation did not note  any cognitive visual or auditory  impairments we reached out for comment  from the wheelchair service contractor  but have not heard back the family's  wrongful deaths complaint does not  specify any monetary damages but it says  Cocoa's medical bills from the fall  totalled nearly $300,000 Dana  Adrianna thank you hard to get those  images out of your mind of her on  as a family and people around trying to  help her
 

